        <!-- ===== Legend on the right ===== -->
        <mxCell id="legend-bg" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EDF3FF;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingTop=10;spacingLeft=20;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#232F3E;" value="Numbered flow steps" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1730" y="140" width="640" height="1180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend-body" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=13;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#232F3E;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[1]&lt;/b&gt; Customer → Amazon Connect. Voice call (PSTN) or Connect Chat message; DNIS resolves tenant.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[1']&lt;/b&gt; Customer → API Gateway. Web / mobile POST to /assistant/chat; Cognito JWT authorizer.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[2]&lt;/b&gt; Amazon Connect → Supervisor Lambda. Tenant-branded contact flow invokes the Lambda integration.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[2']&lt;/b&gt; API Gateway → Supervisor Lambda. REST proxy forwards to the same Lambda that Connect uses.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[3]&lt;/b&gt; Supervisor Lambda → AgentCore Runtime. Invokes vsa_supervisor_bidi_* (voice) or vsa_supervisor_text_* (chat/web).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[4]&lt;/b&gt; Session-init grounding (folded — full detail on Diagram 2). AgentCore Runtime fans out to CMS Redis LKS + Centralized Data Repository + AgentCore Memory.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[5]&lt;/b&gt; AgentCore Runtime → Triage Classifier. Deterministic P0/P1/P2/P3 rules engine over DTCs + telemetry + recalls + tenant policy overrides.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[6/7/8/9]&lt;/b&gt; Per-turn grounding (folded — full detail on Diagram 2). AgentCore Memory reads [6], Bedrock KB Retrieve [7], CMS Recalls [8], CMS DynamoDB write on book() [9].&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[10]&lt;/b&gt; Escalation (folded — full detail on Diagram 3). Triggered when triage() returns P0/P1/P2 or on explicit customer request.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[12]&lt;/b&gt; AgentCore Runtime → Supervisor Lambda. Synthesized grounded response (voice: token stream to Nova 2 Sonic; text: JSON).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[13a]&lt;/b&gt; Supervisor Lambda → Amazon Connect. Voice: Nova 2 Sonic audio via Connect. Chat: text via Connect Chat WebSocket.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[13b]&lt;/b&gt; Supervisor Lambda → API Gateway. Web / mobile JSON response with text + triage + vin + citations fields.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;[14]&lt;/b&gt; Amazon Connect / API Gateway → Customer. End-to-end response delivered on the same channel the customer entered on.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1750" y="185" width="605" height="1120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

